{"id": "a01_terrain", "scores": [5, 6, 4], "final": "needs-lead-review", "issues": ["Fix palette key typo in `tree_3` trunk which uses snow/stone colors (`Z`, `Q`) instead of brown wood tones (`b`, `B`, `t`, `T`), causing bright white/grey vertical stripes on the trunk.", "Replace concentric ring ('pillow shading') on trees, rocks, and mountains with unified top-left directional lighting and proper highlight/shadow zones.", "Redesign `tile_forest`, `tile_rock`, `tile_mountain`, and `tile_road` to avoid sub-tile 2x2 grid repeating patterns that create ugly checkerboard tiling artifacts when rendered on a map.", "Redesign `tile_road` to visually represent a dirt path/trail rather than isolated polka-dot circles.", "Fix `deco_1`, `deco_2`, and `deco_3` so flower stems and petals form contiguous plants rooted at the base rather than floating disjointed pixels.", "Apply dark 1px outlines (`f` or `g`) around tree canopies and foliage so sprites match the required outline style."]}
{"id": "a02_buildings", "scores": [5, 5, 4], "final": "needs-lead-review", "issues": ["Replace flat rect fills in drawStoneBlock, drawTimberWall, and roofs with layered brick/timber/tile textures and top-left specular highlights to meet the 4-6 tone per material requirement.", "Redesign drawPitchedRoof and drawThatchRoof to render actual tile courses and thatched straw texture instead of solid flat-color triangles.", "Rework b_tower banner logic so the flag attaches to a visible flagpole rather than rendering as a floating blue rectangle on the wall.", "Make scaffold sprites distinct for each building by rendering unique partial masonry/framing under construction rather than relying on a uniform generic scaffold grid with minimal prop overlays.", "Add top-left light-source shading and cast shadows on all wall extrusions, doors, and chimneys to remove the flat blocky programmer-art look."]}
{"id": "a03_settlers", "scores": [5, 4, 6], "final": "needs-lead-review", "issues": ["Material shading lacks depth: tunics and skin use only 2 color tones instead of the required warm 4-6 tone palette with consistent top-left lighting.", "Hard hat accessory rendered as a flat yellow band without a curved 3D brim or proper highlight/shadow structure.", "Builder hammer sprite component floats behind the body without a defined arm or hands holding it.", "Walk animation leg frames appear detached from the tunic baseline; add cast shadows on legs under the tunic hem for grounded depth.", "Tunic side shading contains isolated single-pixel shadow spots instead of directional rim lighting from the top-left light source."]}
